        "note": "Salesforce Composite's lesson: outer success is not subrequest success. success=false for the document, b1 committed with its counts, b2 rolled back — every reporting layer says its own thing and the runner reads all of them. b1's rows are addressed by id because b2's edge must name them: a ref of another batch is not addressable (refs are batch-local, and an assigned id is not known until the import returns)."
